    <description>Quick Action screen flow on Opportunity. Requires at least one Opportunity Line Item flagged AF_RequiresInternalRequisition__c before allowing the request (accessories/PDI requirements must be selected first, per BRD). 2026-09-17: added a second gate - at least one Quote must exist on the Opportunity (Quote.OpportunityId lookup) - per business decision that the Internal Requisition request should only become available once a Quote has been created, in addition to the existing line-item flag requirement (both gates apply, neither replaces the other). Captures the requested completion date, sets AF_RequisitionStatus__c = Pending Approval, then submits for approval via AF_AP_Opp_InternalRequisition (Sales Manager approval, routed via the owner&apos;s manager). Same manager-hierarchy submission pattern as AF_FL_Opp_RequestClosure. LFRDN-748 (2026-09-27): the flow never checked AF_RequisitionStatus__c before running - a second request while one was already Pending Approval reached Update_Opportunity, which failed on the approval process&apos;s own record lock (ENTITY_IS_LOCKED) and surfaced that raw SOAP exception code to the rep via $Flow.FaultMessage. Added an up-front status check that shows a plain &quot;already pending&quot; message instead of ever reaching the update.

LFRDN-761 fix: added Share_Opportunity_With_Manager (same OpportunityShare/Edit/Manual pattern as LFRDN-707/728/762) right after Update_Opportunity, before Submit_For_Approval - the resolved Manager may be outside the Opportunity&apos;s BU and have no sharing access otherwise.</description>
